    {
      "id": "claim_08f11361c4ff43879ad272ea87e45660",
      "statement": "The interestScoringExecutor bean (InterestScoringConfig) is a dedicated ThreadPoolTaskExecutor with core pool size = max pool size = myfeeder.interest.concurrency (default 1) and queue-capacity 1000 (default), named jev-score-, registered with defaultCandidate=false so it does not replace Boot's applicationTaskExecutor, injected only via @Qualifier, with no @Async usage anywhere in the scoring path; it intentionally keeps the default abort rejection policy because ScoringQueue depends on catching TaskRejectedException to release ids.",
      "evidence": [
