      "statement": "POST /api/interest/rescore only accepts application/json (rejecting a cross-site bodyless/form/text POST with 415), requires confirm:true in the body (400 otherwise), and InterestRescoreService.rescore() throws a fixed-text IllegalStateException mapped to 409 when Jev is unconfigured or the rubric is in cold start; the Re-score scope and its count share one predicate (eligible articles with a SCORED or FAILED row, SKIPPED excluded) so the confirmation count matches exactly what gets deleted, and deleted rows are not immediately re-scored but become eligible for the next sweep or ingest.",
